1
00:00:01,435 --> 00:00:03,403
EPISODE 4

2
00:00:14,581 --> 00:00:17,618
I'm sorry. Please forgive me.

3
00:00:26,093 --> 00:00:27,661
Hey, turn off the heater.

4
00:00:29,096 --> 00:00:30,998
Turn off the heater!

5
00:00:31,732 --> 00:00:34,902
Hey, fire! Fire, fire!

6
00:00:34,968 --> 00:00:37,538
Put it out! Put out the fire!

7
00:00:44,945 --> 00:00:47,347
-Water! Water!
-Water! Water! Water!

8
00:00:48,982 --> 00:00:50,751
What do we do?

9
00:00:50,817 --> 00:00:51,685
No water!

10
00:00:51,752 --> 00:00:53,387
-Why not?
-I don't know!

11
00:00:53,453 --> 00:00:55,088
Man-gu! Mr. Man-gu!

12
00:00:55,155 --> 00:00:57,558
He really cut off our water!
What do we do?

13
00:00:57,624 --> 00:00:59,126
What do we do?

14
00:00:59,826 --> 00:01:01,695
Grab the instruments first!

15
00:01:01,762 --> 00:01:03,697
Get the instruments first!

16
00:01:05,465 --> 00:01:08,235
Ow, it's hot! So hot!

17
00:01:08,302 --> 00:01:10,971
-Hurry up!
-My drums! Where are my drums?

18
00:01:14,841 --> 00:01:17,010
Stop it, you idiot! Hurry!

19
00:01:18,879 --> 00:01:22,015
-Grab the clothes, hurry!
-Clothes! Clothes!

20
00:01:34,027 --> 00:01:37,197
Now these punks are
setting the house on fire?

21
00:01:37,264 --> 00:01:40,467
Look at these crazy fools.
Why, I oughta…

22
00:01:40,534 --> 00:01:43,070
Leave them be.

23
00:01:43,136 --> 00:01:44,304
This is for the best.

24
00:01:44,371 --> 00:01:47,507
We won't even have to kick them out.
They'll leave on their own.

25
00:01:47,574 --> 00:01:51,311
Now I can finally sleep
in total peace.

26
00:01:52,846 --> 00:01:54,748
Those rotten punks.

27
00:02:22,042 --> 00:02:23,377
Let's just quit now.

28
00:02:25,178 --> 00:02:28,715
Right, it's all over.

29
00:02:29,883 --> 00:02:33,587
Right, this is a sign from above.

30
00:02:36,323 --> 00:02:39,126
No, I'll never give up,
even if it kills me.

31
00:02:39,926 --> 00:02:41,128
I'm never giving up!

32
00:02:41,194 --> 00:02:43,630
We don't even have a house.
What'll you do?

33
00:02:47,434 --> 00:02:49,569
We still have one last hope.

34
00:02:51,038 --> 00:02:52,706
Just trust me.

35
00:02:55,375 --> 00:02:57,044
Go on, then.

36
00:03:05,185 --> 00:03:07,654
So, you're gonna enter
the township sports day?

37
00:03:08,689 --> 00:03:12,559
We'll win it for you, no question.

38
00:03:13,660 --> 00:03:16,663
Hyeok trained at the
Cha Bum-kun Football Club,

39
00:03:16,730 --> 00:03:18,532
was a striker through high school,

40
00:03:18,598 --> 00:03:23,470
and Ki-jun was the division
foot-volleyball king in the army.

41
00:03:24,237 --> 00:03:25,739
And as for Han-cheol…

42
00:03:30,310 --> 00:03:32,079
he's strong.

43
00:03:32,145 --> 00:03:33,613
Smart, too.

44
00:03:34,681 --> 00:03:36,550
And as for me…

45
00:03:36,616 --> 00:03:38,985
I'm an all-around athlete
who's good at everything,

46
00:03:39,052 --> 00:03:40,620
as you well know.

47
00:03:40,687 --> 00:03:41,588
Your terms?

48
00:03:41,655 --> 00:03:43,857
Room and board.

49
00:03:43,924 --> 00:03:45,525
Just till the cabbage harvest.

50
00:03:49,930 --> 00:03:52,165
Are you really sure
you can win this?

51
00:03:52,232 --> 00:03:53,633
Don't worry.

52
00:03:53,700 --> 00:03:55,335
We're in our fiery twenties.

53
00:03:55,402 --> 00:03:56,937
Young enough to chew steel.

54
00:03:57,003 --> 00:04:01,108
We couldn't lose to those old geezers
in their fifties if we tried.

55
00:04:01,174 --> 00:04:02,342
What do you call it?

56
00:04:02,409 --> 00:04:04,845
Easier than taking candy
from a baby?

57
00:04:04,911 --> 00:04:07,247
Don't underestimate
Sangdurok-ri like that.

58
00:04:08,215 --> 00:04:10,584
Sangdurok-ri won last year,
the year before,

59
00:04:10,650 --> 00:04:12,152
the year before that,

60
00:04:12,219 --> 00:04:13,887
and the year before…

61
00:04:13,954 --> 00:04:16,456
Anyway, they've won
nine years in a row.

62
00:04:16,523 --> 00:04:19,392
Starting with an ex-pro soccer player
who moved there to farm,

63
00:04:19,459 --> 00:04:20,494
2012 SPORTS DAY
CHAMPIONS

64
00:04:20,560 --> 00:04:23,296
that village is packed
with total pros.

65
00:04:23,363 --> 00:04:25,031
In soccer terms,

66
00:04:25,098 --> 00:04:28,135
they're a super team
like Real Madrid.

67
00:04:28,201 --> 00:04:29,870
Plus, the Sangdurok-ri Village Head

68
00:04:29,936 --> 00:04:32,072
is the top strategist in our township

69
00:04:32,139 --> 00:04:33,974
and famous for his massive charisma.

70
00:04:34,040 --> 00:04:35,342
SUPREME ABOVE ALL

71
00:04:36,109 --> 00:04:37,844
Still think you can do it?

72
00:04:37,911 --> 00:04:39,646
Don't worry.

73
00:04:39,713 --> 00:04:41,615
We're on the edge of a cliff, too.

74
00:04:41,681 --> 00:04:43,416
We have nowhere left to retreat.

75
00:04:44,417 --> 00:04:47,687
Then we have a deal.

76
00:04:57,764 --> 00:04:59,533
Ow, that stings.

77
00:05:03,904 --> 00:05:04,871
Hmph.

78
00:05:06,606 --> 00:05:11,178
Honey, you've washed the baby enough.
Check your husband's finger too.

79
00:05:11,244 --> 00:05:13,513
Honestly, you…

80
00:05:13,580 --> 00:05:16,149
You find the wildest ways
to get hurt.

81
00:05:16,216 --> 00:05:18,652
How do you sprain a finger
playing a phone game?

82
00:05:18,718 --> 00:05:22,055
The monster was trying to eat me!
What else could I do?

83
00:05:22,122 --> 00:05:26,426
At a time like that,
you grab the cell phone

84
00:05:26,493 --> 00:05:30,063
and mash the button like this
to get away!

85
00:05:31,231 --> 00:05:32,632
I'm back.

86
00:05:32,699 --> 00:05:34,501
Where did you go so early…

87
00:05:35,502 --> 00:05:37,838
What are you punks doing here?

88
00:05:37,904 --> 00:05:40,907
They're staying at our place
for a while starting today.

89
00:05:40,974 --> 00:05:42,576
-What?
-Hey, say hello.

90
00:05:42,642 --> 00:05:44,177
My uncle and aunt.

91
00:05:44,244 --> 00:05:47,013
Hello. Thanks for having us.

92
00:05:47,080 --> 00:05:50,517
Having you? What are you
talking about right now?

93
00:05:50,584 --> 00:05:53,019
I'll explain everything later, okay?

94
00:05:53,787 --> 00:05:55,422
Hey, follow me.

95
00:06:09,603 --> 00:06:10,904
In here.

96
00:06:12,672 --> 00:06:14,207
Wait, this tiny little…

97
00:06:14,274 --> 00:06:16,610
You want the four of us
to sleep in a room like this?

98
00:06:16,676 --> 00:06:20,313
Then go back to Seoul right now.

99
00:06:20,380 --> 00:06:23,583
Five of us could easily
sleep in here, yep.

100
00:06:23,650 --> 00:06:26,987
Anyway, if you burn this place down,
you're dead.

101
00:06:27,954 --> 00:06:29,256
Um, Yun-hui…

102
00:06:29,322 --> 00:06:31,224
Uh, by any chance…

103
00:06:32,492 --> 00:06:34,461
Could you lend us some clothes?

104
00:06:34,527 --> 00:06:38,164
As you can see,
all our clothes burned up.

105
00:06:43,970 --> 00:06:45,739
Gosh, move.

106
00:06:45,805 --> 00:06:47,540
Move, move, move!

107
00:06:47,607 --> 00:06:49,376
Take care, ma'am.

108
00:06:51,578 --> 00:06:54,214
Ugh, that smell! What is that smell?

109
00:06:54,848 --> 00:06:57,384
There's mold everywhere, everywhere.

110
00:07:00,387 --> 00:07:04,591
Did an artisan from the Spring and Autumn
and Warring States Period do this

111
00:07:05,659 --> 00:07:08,194
stitch by stitch?
And why's it that color?

112
00:07:09,863 --> 00:07:11,665
A moth…

113
00:07:16,970 --> 00:07:20,073
How did we end up like this?

114
00:07:20,140 --> 00:07:22,409
What disaster are you inviting,

115
00:07:22,475 --> 00:07:24,277
bringing those crazy bastards
into the house?

116
00:07:24,344 --> 00:07:28,048
How dare they crawl into this house?

117
00:07:28,114 --> 00:07:30,483
Keep your voice down.
The boys will hear you.

118
00:07:30,550 --> 00:07:33,086
I'm whispering!
How could they hear me?

119
00:07:33,153 --> 00:07:35,822
We hear everything! We can hear you!

120
00:07:35,889 --> 00:07:37,257
Oh, you can?

121
00:07:37,324 --> 00:07:40,060
This is driving me crazy, jeez.

122
00:07:47,534 --> 00:07:49,235
It's okay, it's okay.

123
00:07:49,302 --> 00:07:51,338
What's okay about this?

124
00:07:51,404 --> 00:07:52,872
Even this crummy room,

125
00:07:52,939 --> 00:07:55,342
you said we have to vacate it
if we don't win sports day!

126
00:07:55,408 --> 00:07:58,578
Why did I follow you here?
What is this?

127
00:07:58,645 --> 00:08:00,280
I miss my mom all of a sudden.

128
00:08:02,148 --> 00:08:03,717
Don't touch me, jeez.

129
00:08:27,207 --> 00:08:32,112
What's wrong? Didn't sleep well?
Was your bed uncomfortable?

130
00:08:33,046 --> 00:08:36,883
No, I barely slept because
I was planning my mural all night.

131
00:08:36,950 --> 00:08:38,084
Really?

132
00:08:38,151 --> 00:08:40,153
So you're painting starting today?

133
00:08:40,220 --> 00:08:44,124
What? Oh, yes, I should.

134
00:08:45,091 --> 00:08:46,559
Thank you for the meal.

135
00:08:46,626 --> 00:08:48,194
Ma'am, I'll do the dishes.

136
00:08:48,261 --> 00:08:50,864
No, no, I'll do them.
Go inside and rest.

137
00:08:50,930 --> 00:08:51,931
You have to paint.

138
00:08:51,998 --> 00:08:54,968
No, I already feel bad
eating and staying here for free.

139
00:08:55,035 --> 00:08:57,537
-I should do the dishes.
-I told you it's fine.

140
00:08:57,604 --> 00:09:01,341
Well, since you insist so much,
I guess I have no choice.

141
00:09:01,408 --> 00:09:02,942
Enjoy the rest of your meal.

142
00:09:07,614 --> 00:09:10,383
Wow, how can someone so young

143
00:09:10,450 --> 00:09:12,619
be so pretty and well-mannered?

144
00:09:12,685 --> 00:09:13,853
I'd love to have her.

145
00:09:16,389 --> 00:09:20,026
If you want her so badly,
have another son right now.

146
00:09:21,194 --> 00:09:23,763
I'm not interested in her.

147
00:09:23,830 --> 00:09:25,532
She's not my type.

148
00:09:27,400 --> 00:09:29,702
Are you in any position
to be picky about types?

149
00:09:29,769 --> 00:09:32,105
And how can you stomach that
first thing in the morning?

150
00:09:33,239 --> 00:09:35,008
It's a meal and a drink in one.

151
00:09:35,075 --> 00:09:36,576
It gets me buzzed and full.

152
00:09:36,643 --> 00:09:39,045
It saves time and feels great.

153
00:09:39,112 --> 00:09:41,548
Gosh, you drive me up the wall!

154
00:09:42,348 --> 00:09:44,184
-Father!
-Huh? What?

155
00:09:46,352 --> 00:09:48,088
This is driving me crazy!

156
00:09:56,696 --> 00:09:59,399
Darn it, I'm so exhausted.

157
00:10:14,180 --> 00:10:15,048
SCREEN CAPTION

158
00:10:21,054 --> 00:10:23,056
Oh, my aching head.

159
00:10:26,292 --> 00:10:27,594
Hello?

160
00:10:27,660 --> 00:10:29,229
Hey, it's me.

161
00:10:30,497 --> 00:10:32,165
Who is this?

162
00:10:32,232 --> 00:10:34,601
Passed out drunk at the bar
instead of going home again.

163
00:10:34,667 --> 00:10:36,703
Is that you, Su-yeon?

164
00:10:36,769 --> 00:10:38,338
Hey, bitch, where are you?

165
00:10:38,404 --> 00:10:40,440
You ditched work
and changed your number!

166
00:10:40,507 --> 00:10:42,175
Sorry, something came up.

167
00:10:42,842 --> 00:10:44,310
Um, listen.

168
00:10:44,377 --> 00:10:46,679
Settle my pay for this month
and wire it to my account.

169
00:10:46,746 --> 00:10:48,615
I need a little cash.

170
00:10:48,681 --> 00:10:50,416
Look at this shameless bitch.

171
00:10:50,483 --> 00:10:53,186
Do you know how much money
I lost because of you, bitch?

172
00:10:55,221 --> 00:10:56,890
Right.

173
00:10:56,956 --> 00:10:58,258
But…

174
00:10:58,324 --> 00:11:02,195
things will get pretty messy if the
cops find out you sell fake liquor.

175
00:11:02,862 --> 00:11:04,697
-Right?
-What?

176
00:11:04,764 --> 00:11:07,367
What do you mean, fake liquor?

177
00:11:08,201 --> 00:11:11,704
We only sell the real stuff, you brat!

178
00:11:11,771 --> 00:11:13,106
Who are you kidding?

179
00:11:13,173 --> 00:11:15,875
The liquor I've chugged could circle
Jamsil Main Stadium five rows deep.

180
00:11:15,942 --> 00:11:16,976
Cut the crap.

181
00:11:17,043 --> 00:11:19,579
Plus, sticking wasted guys
with fake bar tabs.

182
00:11:19,646 --> 00:11:22,115
Tax evasion, letting minors in.

183
00:11:22,182 --> 00:11:23,550
And what else!

184
00:11:23,616 --> 00:11:27,287
Okay, fine, fine!
I'll send it, you bitch!

185
00:11:27,353 --> 00:11:29,355
Jeez, what a scary bitch.

186
00:11:29,422 --> 00:11:32,692
See? Why push a nice girl
to play dirty?

187
00:11:32,759 --> 00:11:35,595
You were always nasty.

188
00:11:35,662 --> 00:11:38,831
Anyway, why did you quit the bar
all of a sudden?

189
00:11:39,332 --> 00:11:41,201
Busted moonlighting at your day job?

190
00:11:41,267 --> 00:11:43,903
I quit my day job too.

191
00:11:43,970 --> 00:11:45,538
I'll explain this later.

192
00:11:46,606 --> 00:11:48,541
You're like an onion, bitch.

193
00:11:48,608 --> 00:11:51,344
I peel and peel,
and still can't figure you out.

194
00:11:51,411 --> 00:11:53,246
Anyway, I'll call you again,

195
00:11:53,313 --> 00:11:56,115
so wire the money by today.
Got it?

196
00:12:00,153 --> 00:12:02,322
Darn it, I should've said
I came to rest.

197
00:12:02,388 --> 00:12:03,756
Why'd I say I'd paint murals?

198
00:12:03,823 --> 00:12:05,658
I'm just blowing my money, darn it.

199
00:12:10,530 --> 00:12:12,432
-What is this?
-You asked for clothes.

200
00:12:15,935 --> 00:12:18,871
Yun-hui, we're rockers! Rockers!

201
00:12:18,938 --> 00:12:22,108
We're practically celebrities
in pop culture!

202
00:12:22,175 --> 00:12:24,010
And you want us to wear this junk?

203
00:12:24,611 --> 00:12:27,046
Suit yourself, then.

204
00:12:28,248 --> 00:12:30,049
Oh, no, wait!

205
00:12:30,116 --> 00:12:31,884
Wow, these clothes are so pretty!

206
00:12:31,951 --> 00:12:34,220
We'll gladly wear them.
Thank you so much.

207
00:12:35,488 --> 00:12:37,724
Thank you, we'll wear them well.

208
00:12:40,693 --> 00:12:42,962
Yes, take care, ma'am.
Take care.

209
00:12:45,798 --> 00:12:50,203
I'd rather die
than wear this garbage.

210
00:12:53,373 --> 00:12:56,009
Min-ho, don't lose these.
Make sure you bring them home, okay?

211
00:12:56,075 --> 00:12:57,310
Okay.

212
00:13:05,618 --> 00:13:07,320
Hey, Min-ho.

213
00:13:07,387 --> 00:13:10,556
Hey, those really suit you guys!

214
00:13:10,623 --> 00:13:12,825
Now you look like real farmers!

215
00:13:14,060 --> 00:13:18,131
Stop laughing.
This is driving me nuts.

216
00:13:19,932 --> 00:13:22,035
-Aren't you feeding us?
-Food? We already ate.

217
00:13:22,101 --> 00:13:24,037
Already?
It's only eight o'clock.

218
00:13:24,103 --> 00:13:26,706
Oh, you didn't know.
Here, breakfast is at five,

219
00:13:26,773 --> 00:13:29,042
lunch at 11, dinner at five.
Remember that.

220
00:13:29,108 --> 00:13:32,545
What? You eat breakfast
at five in the morning?

221
00:13:32,612 --> 00:13:35,481
We have to eat early
to work while it's cool.

222
00:13:35,548 --> 00:13:37,684
Don't you know it's too hot
to work once the sun's up?

223
00:13:37,750 --> 00:13:39,886
Also, the farm tools
are in that shed,

224
00:13:39,952 --> 00:13:41,988
so help yourselves to them,

225
00:13:42,055 --> 00:13:44,924
wash them spotless,
and put them right back.

226
00:13:44,991 --> 00:13:48,194
If even one goes missing,
I'm charging you for it.

227
00:13:48,261 --> 00:13:50,163
Why did you get so ruthless?

228
00:13:50,229 --> 00:13:52,665
Where did the Kang Yun-hui
I knew go!

229
00:13:53,399 --> 00:13:57,136
The Kang Yun-hui you knew is dead.
Forget her.

230
00:13:57,203 --> 00:14:00,273
Min-ho, let's go.
I'll walk you to school.

231
00:14:00,340 --> 00:14:01,474
Oh, right.

232
00:14:02,408 --> 00:14:05,912
We're practicing after lunch,
so meet at the branch school field.

233
00:14:06,479 --> 00:14:09,949
Be even a second late,
and I'll kick you all out!

234
00:14:10,016 --> 00:14:11,484
Yes, ma'am.

235
00:14:15,455 --> 00:14:18,591
Jeez, she's ruthless.

236
00:14:18,658 --> 00:14:20,960
How can a person
change like that?

237
00:14:21,027 --> 00:14:23,629
She said the first love you knew
is dead, man.

238
00:14:24,664 --> 00:14:28,201
Still, the more you see her,
isn't she a total trip?

239
00:14:29,001 --> 00:14:30,002
She's got charm.

240
00:14:30,069 --> 00:14:32,305
Charm, my foot.

241
00:14:32,372 --> 00:14:34,107
She's like an old witch.

242
00:14:40,713 --> 00:14:43,883
What trouble are you inviting
letting an outsider in?

243
00:14:43,950 --> 00:14:46,519
I told you, this young lady
is here to volunteer.

244
00:14:46,586 --> 00:14:49,789
Volunteer, my foot! Are we beggars?

245
00:14:49,856 --> 00:14:53,459
Listen, miss.
Just behave yourself while you're here.

246
00:14:53,526 --> 00:14:56,529
If I catch you pulling anything funny,
you're out right away.

247
00:14:57,430 --> 00:14:59,866
Yes, don't worry.

248
00:15:12,912 --> 00:15:14,547
Darn it, what kind of town is this?

249
00:15:14,614 --> 00:15:17,049
They're so disgustingly petty,
I don't even want to volunteer.

250
00:15:20,219 --> 00:15:22,088
-It's so heavy.
-Mister, get off.

251
00:15:22,155 --> 00:15:24,390
-Hey, I'm sick.
-Are you really not getting off?

252
00:15:24,457 --> 00:15:26,392
-Knock it off.
-Wait.

253
00:15:26,459 --> 00:15:29,362
Wait, this town had
such a pure, innocent woman?

254
00:15:31,664 --> 00:15:33,733
Hello.

255
00:15:33,800 --> 00:15:35,468
We just moved here recently…

256
00:15:35,535 --> 00:15:37,069
It's coming now!

257
00:15:39,372 --> 00:15:41,007
What a relief.

258
00:15:42,775 --> 00:15:43,943
Hello.

259
00:15:44,010 --> 00:15:45,511
Hey, say hello.

260
00:15:48,648 --> 00:15:50,149
What? Where's she going?

261
00:15:50,216 --> 00:15:51,384
Why'd she run away?

262
00:15:51,451 --> 00:15:52,985
It's because of you.

263
00:15:53,052 --> 00:15:54,720
-My face?
-You look so greasy.

264
00:15:54,787 --> 00:15:56,789
-Come on, let's keep moving.
-Let's go.

265
00:15:57,356 --> 00:15:58,524
Let's go.

266
00:15:59,492 --> 00:16:01,260
Hey, are you really not getting off?

267
00:16:07,733 --> 00:16:10,169
Hey, what on earth is wrong with you?

268
00:16:10,236 --> 00:16:11,938
Who is that woman anyway?

269
00:16:12,004 --> 00:16:15,875
Wait, was that the woman
you told us about?

270
00:16:15,942 --> 00:16:17,944
Love at first sight?

271
00:16:18,010 --> 00:16:21,180
Then why the long face?
Did something happen?

272
00:16:23,182 --> 00:16:26,752
Hold on, something really
did happen to him.

273
00:16:26,819 --> 00:16:30,122
Don't agonize over it alone.
Tell us.

274
00:16:30,189 --> 00:16:31,858
Right, man.

275
00:16:34,994 --> 00:16:36,963
Guys…

276
00:16:37,029 --> 00:16:40,500
The truth is, um…

277
00:16:44,103 --> 00:16:45,204
What?

278
00:16:46,172 --> 00:16:49,208
So in front of that woman,

279
00:16:50,710 --> 00:16:51,844
you took a dump?

280
00:16:53,112 --> 00:16:55,214
And with no toilet paper,

281
00:16:55,281 --> 00:16:58,451
you tumbled over
taking your socks off?

282
00:16:59,819 --> 00:17:03,723
With… with your pants
all the way down?

283
00:17:08,427 --> 00:17:10,029
-What do we do?
-What now?

284
00:17:10,096 --> 00:17:12,031
There's no hope. No hope at all.

285
00:17:12,098 --> 00:17:14,233
It's all over.

286
00:17:14,300 --> 00:17:18,404
I'm packing up and going back to Seoul.

287
00:17:18,471 --> 00:17:20,573
What kind of nonsense is that?

288
00:17:20,640 --> 00:17:24,010
I can't live in the same town
and face her, not me.

289
00:17:25,778 --> 00:17:28,848
Come on, you're a man!
Why let that get to you?

290
00:17:28,915 --> 00:17:30,082
What's the big deal?

291
00:17:31,951 --> 00:17:33,686
My friends…

292
00:17:33,753 --> 00:17:37,623
They say a bad first impression
means a 99.99999% chance of failure.

293
00:17:37,690 --> 00:17:39,392
There are studies on it!

294
00:17:40,626 --> 00:17:43,596
And in front of that woman…

295
00:17:43,663 --> 00:17:45,932
I took a dump! A dump!

296
00:17:45,998 --> 00:17:50,469
Still, it's a natural bodily function.
She'll understand.

297
00:17:53,039 --> 00:17:54,407
Right, of course.

298
00:17:54,473 --> 00:17:55,708
Right, sure.

299
00:17:55,775 --> 00:17:58,210
Just a bodily function
everybody has.

300
00:17:58,277 --> 00:18:00,947
Okay, then say you're on a blind date.

301
00:18:01,013 --> 00:18:03,516
But nature calls so urgently for her

302
00:18:03,583 --> 00:18:05,618
that she poops right in front of you.

303
00:18:05,685 --> 00:18:07,386
Now, you'll keep dating her, right?

304
00:18:07,453 --> 00:18:08,421
Are you crazy?

305
00:18:08,487 --> 00:18:09,922
-You jerk!
-Hey, hey!

306
00:18:09,989 --> 00:18:11,791
-Let go!
-Hey, sit down. Calm down.

307
00:18:11,857 --> 00:18:14,794
See, you jerk?
You can't understand it either!

308
00:18:14,860 --> 00:18:16,162
Seriously, man…

309
00:18:17,063 --> 00:18:19,332
My first and last love

310
00:18:20,099 --> 00:18:21,968
draws the curtain so hideously.

311
00:18:22,034 --> 00:18:23,269
Last love, my foot.

312
00:18:23,336 --> 00:18:25,972
Cheol, there are plenty of fish
in the sea.

313
00:18:26,038 --> 00:18:28,674
Right, half the world is women.

314
00:18:29,241 --> 00:18:32,311
But the only woman I like
is her, only her.

315
00:18:32,378 --> 00:18:36,616
And I don't have time
to meet another woman.

316
00:18:36,682 --> 00:18:38,017
I have no time.

317
00:18:38,084 --> 00:18:40,553
What? Why not?
We have all the time in the world.

318
00:18:42,188 --> 00:18:45,124
Do you guys know how I feel?
Hey, you guys…

319
00:18:46,025 --> 00:18:47,760
You don't know how I feel!

320
00:18:47,827 --> 00:18:50,963
You have no idea how I feel,
you jerks! Seriously!

321
00:18:51,664 --> 00:18:53,966
-Where are you going?
-Don't call me!

322
00:18:54,033 --> 00:18:55,901
What's really wrong with him lately?

323
00:18:56,569 --> 00:18:58,270
Big fuss over first love, right?

324
00:19:02,308 --> 00:19:04,777
Hey, Ki-jun, your girlfriend's here.

325
00:19:04,844 --> 00:19:06,212
Seriously, knock it off…

326
00:19:06,278 --> 00:19:07,380
Sister-in-law?

327
00:19:08,748 --> 00:19:10,316
What is this?

328
00:19:10,383 --> 00:19:12,885
It's nothing special.
Just have a taste.

329
00:19:12,952 --> 00:19:15,321
What is this, though?

330
00:19:16,322 --> 00:19:18,224
Wait, excuse me!

331
00:19:18,290 --> 00:19:19,825
She's driving me crazy.

332
00:19:19,892 --> 00:19:21,427
What is this?

333
00:19:21,494 --> 00:19:22,895
Give it here.

334
00:19:23,663 --> 00:19:25,698
These are pine mushrooms!

335
00:19:28,200 --> 00:19:30,803
-They look like wild pine mushrooms.
-Wild ones?

336
00:19:30,870 --> 00:19:32,605
They're huge in this town.

337
00:19:32,672 --> 00:19:35,408
-Really?
-Wow, these are super expensive.

338
00:19:36,075 --> 00:19:37,777
She really must like you, man.

339
00:19:37,843 --> 00:19:40,379
Nonsense! She doesn't like me.
Just stop it!

340
00:19:42,048 --> 00:19:43,916
Ramen? Seriously, ramen?

341
00:19:43,983 --> 00:19:46,152
How can we work on just ramen?

342
00:19:46,218 --> 00:19:49,455
Eating your ramen quietly
will be good for your own health.

343
00:19:49,522 --> 00:19:52,525
My aunt's cooking is
absolutely atrocious.

344
00:19:52,591 --> 00:19:53,826
Yeah, right.

345
00:19:53,893 --> 00:19:56,729
Making up all kinds of excuses
to save on meal money.

346
00:19:56,796 --> 00:19:59,565
Hey, walk faster!
The village elders are waiting.

347
00:19:59,632 --> 00:20:00,800
We're walking fast!

348
00:20:01,901 --> 00:20:03,536
What's taking them so long?

349
00:20:04,670 --> 00:20:06,706
If you make a promise, keep it.

350
00:20:08,174 --> 00:20:10,209
Are we doing this or what?

351
00:20:10,276 --> 00:20:11,911
Hey, hurry up!

352
00:20:13,713 --> 00:20:15,314
There they are.

353
00:20:15,381 --> 00:20:17,483
We're late. I'm so sorry.

354
00:20:17,550 --> 00:20:20,386
-Who are those punks?
-Hey, hurry up and get over here!

355
00:20:20,453 --> 00:20:21,921
Why are those punks coming?

356
00:20:21,987 --> 00:20:23,723
I apologize.

357
00:20:23,789 --> 00:20:25,858
I'm so sorry. I'm late.

358
00:20:25,925 --> 00:20:28,561
Forget sorry.
Why did you bring these punks?

359
00:20:28,627 --> 00:20:31,564
They agreed to compete
in the sports day too.

360
00:20:31,630 --> 00:20:34,333
What kind of nonsense is that?
Are you crazy?

361
00:20:34,400 --> 00:20:36,902
Please don't lose your temper first,

362
00:20:36,969 --> 00:20:38,504
and just hear me out.

363
00:20:38,571 --> 00:20:41,474
I don't want to see their pathetic
faces for another second either.

364
00:20:41,540 --> 00:20:42,742
And?

365
00:20:42,808 --> 00:20:45,611
In Sangdurok-ri, our sworn enemy
and eternal rival,

366
00:20:45,678 --> 00:20:48,280
you all know it's packed
with energetic young farmers, right?

367
00:20:48,347 --> 00:20:50,049
Even so…

368
00:20:50,116 --> 00:20:51,450
Don't you know them?

369
00:20:51,517 --> 00:20:53,853
Have you all forgotten

370
00:20:53,919 --> 00:20:56,622
all the atrocities
Sangdurok-ri committed against us?

371
00:21:03,562 --> 00:21:06,599
I know I'm in no position
to step in,

372
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:11,670
but what on earth happened
with Sangdurok-ri

373
00:21:11,737 --> 00:21:14,173
that everyone's out for their blood?

374
00:21:16,208 --> 00:21:19,979
It's a long story,
but we used to get along.

375
00:21:20,479 --> 00:21:23,616
But the very moment
their current Village Head was elected,

376
00:21:23,682 --> 00:21:25,751
things started going sour.

377
00:21:27,219 --> 00:21:29,955
He was as sneaky and deceitful
as a snake.

378
00:21:30,022 --> 00:21:33,392
Plus, he was sharp as a tack
and a master of dirty tricks.

379
00:21:33,459 --> 00:21:35,895
For example, back then in our village,

380
00:21:35,961 --> 00:21:37,963
a public health center
was set to be built.

381
00:21:38,030 --> 00:21:38,898
HADUROK-RI, CLINIC

382
00:21:38,964 --> 00:21:40,933
But that bastard lobbied
the County Governor

383
00:21:41,000 --> 00:21:41,867
SANGDUROK-RI

384
00:21:41,934 --> 00:21:43,936
and diverted the clinic
to their village.

385
00:21:44,003 --> 00:21:46,872
Lobbied? What kind of lobbying?

386
00:21:46,939 --> 00:21:49,341
Here's what that bastard did.

387
00:21:50,009 --> 00:21:52,411
County Governor,
this is my younger sister.

388
00:21:52,478 --> 00:21:54,380
My, it's a pleasure to meet you.

389
00:21:54,446 --> 00:21:56,182
Yes, nice to meet you.

390
00:21:56,782 --> 00:22:00,519
He set him up on a blind date
with his widowed sister. A blind date!

391
00:22:00,586 --> 00:22:02,488
The County Governor was a widower too.

392
00:22:03,222 --> 00:22:05,891
Then as now, the honey trap
is the ultimate weapon!

393
00:22:05,958 --> 00:22:07,793
That's just the tip of the iceberg.

394
00:22:07,860 --> 00:22:10,563
We were first in line
for road paving, and they stole it!

395
00:22:10,629 --> 00:22:12,698
Because of that,
the bus route changed too!

396
00:22:12,765 --> 00:22:16,569
Our town has one bus stop,
but Sangdurok-ri has two! Two!

397
00:22:16,635 --> 00:22:19,505
Even though our town is way bigger.

398
00:22:22,141 --> 00:22:25,678
On top of that, at their bus stop…

399
00:22:25,744 --> 00:22:26,679
SANGDUROK-RI

400
00:22:26,745 --> 00:22:28,180
They even got a roof! A roof!

401
00:22:28,247 --> 00:22:31,250
While our town only has
one measly sign!

402
00:22:32,017 --> 00:22:33,886
Think that's all?

403
00:22:33,953 --> 00:22:38,557
Even for cell phone reception,
our town only gets two measly bars,

404
00:22:38,624 --> 00:22:41,727
but Sangdurok-ri always gets
full bars! Full bars!

405
00:22:41,794 --> 00:22:44,263
So Sangdurok-ri kept developing,

406
00:22:44,330 --> 00:22:46,498
and Hadurok-ri fell further behind.

407
00:22:46,565 --> 00:22:49,335
Energetic young new farmers

408
00:22:49,401 --> 00:22:51,370
all turned their backs on Hadurok-ri

409
00:22:51,437 --> 00:22:53,205
and flocked to Sangdurok-ri.

410
00:22:53,272 --> 00:22:55,541
Because of that, for nine years
the sports day trophy

411
00:22:55,608 --> 00:22:57,243
has been swept up by them too.

412
00:22:57,309 --> 00:23:00,412
So this time, we must win without fail

413
00:23:00,479 --> 00:23:02,147
and take back that trophy!

414
00:23:02,214 --> 00:23:05,618
Even if we take the trophy back,

415
00:23:05,684 --> 00:23:07,052
nothing changes, right?

416
00:23:07,119 --> 00:23:09,655
It's our pride! Our pride!

417
00:23:09,722 --> 00:23:12,124
Plus, if they win ten years in a row,

418
00:23:12,191 --> 00:23:14,526
Sangdurok-ri keeps the trophy forever!

419
00:23:15,494 --> 00:23:16,996
What is this, the World Cup?

420
00:23:17,062 --> 00:23:19,932
This isn't just a simple
village sports day.

421
00:23:19,999 --> 00:23:22,501
With our residents' pride on the line,

422
00:23:22,568 --> 00:23:26,071
it's a war without gunfire. A war!

423
00:23:27,072 --> 00:23:30,442
So to have them compete
for our village,

424
00:23:30,509 --> 00:23:32,011
I made the decision myself.

425
00:23:32,678 --> 00:23:34,413
For the greater good of the games,

426
00:23:34,480 --> 00:23:35,681
nitpicking over this,

427
00:23:35,748 --> 00:23:37,483
I judged this isn't the time for it.

428
00:23:38,183 --> 00:23:40,519
Besides, if they fail to win it for us,

429
00:23:40,586 --> 00:23:43,555
they agreed to leave the village
on their own two feet.

430
00:23:43,622 --> 00:23:45,991
So please set aside your anger
for a moment,

431
00:23:46,058 --> 00:23:48,394
and let's join forces, okay?

432
00:23:53,999 --> 00:23:56,368
Then I'll take that as everyone's
agreement.

433
00:23:57,136 --> 00:23:59,905
How about we start practicing?

434
00:24:02,875 --> 00:24:05,411
Now, I'll introduce the events first.

435
00:24:05,477 --> 00:24:07,313
The official events this time are

436
00:24:07,379 --> 00:24:09,548
Rubber Shoe Toss,

437
00:24:09,615 --> 00:24:11,550
Hula-Hooping with a Rice Sack,

438
00:24:11,617 --> 00:24:13,319
Wife-Carrying Limbo,

439
00:24:13,385 --> 00:24:15,721
and Ten Elephant Spins
and Eating Rice Cake.

440
00:24:15,788 --> 00:24:18,924
Hold on. Those are
the sports day events?

441
00:24:18,991 --> 00:24:21,360
What is this, a daycare talent show?

442
00:24:21,427 --> 00:24:23,395
Gosh, pipe down.
Just shut up and listen.

443
00:24:24,363 --> 00:24:25,931
And Yut Nori, Korean wrestling,

444
00:24:25,998 --> 00:24:27,433
tug-of-war, soccer.

445
00:24:27,499 --> 00:24:29,868
Besides these, worth the most points,

446
00:24:29,935 --> 00:24:31,370
is the 10-person 11-legged race.

447
00:24:31,437 --> 00:24:35,174
Everyone chosen last time,
please practice on your own.

448
00:24:35,240 --> 00:24:37,409
Hey, split up and coach
them one-on-one.

449
00:24:37,476 --> 00:24:38,978
Okay!

450
00:24:40,012 --> 00:24:40,946
Fine.

451
00:24:47,753 --> 00:24:49,054
Oh, my goodness!

452
00:24:55,461 --> 00:24:57,196
Why are you lifting that sack of rice

453
00:24:57,262 --> 00:24:58,831
while spinning a hula hoop?

454
00:24:58,897 --> 00:25:00,366
It's way too easy without it.

455
00:25:00,432 --> 00:25:03,902
Come on, how can a woman
lift something this heavy?

456
00:25:04,536 --> 00:25:05,571
No way.

457
00:25:10,442 --> 00:25:12,378
All right, over there, over there.

458
00:25:12,444 --> 00:25:15,014
First, bow to each other. Bow.

459
00:25:16,181 --> 00:25:18,550
Okay, n… now sit down.

460
00:25:18,617 --> 00:25:20,753
Sit down. Kneel down on the sand.

461
00:25:20,819 --> 00:25:23,489
In wrestling, whoever grabs
the thigh band tightly

462
00:25:23,555 --> 00:25:25,090
takes control of the match.

463
00:25:25,157 --> 00:25:26,725
Got it? Just hold on tight.

464
00:25:26,792 --> 00:25:29,528
Sir, move in closer. Yes.

465
00:25:34,967 --> 00:25:37,036
That tickles! It tickles, it tickles!

466
00:25:37,102 --> 00:25:40,039
It tickles, it tickles!
I can't do this, I can't!

467
00:25:40,105 --> 00:25:41,740
It tickles, it tickles!

468
00:25:44,076 --> 00:25:46,478
You have to read the direction well.

469
00:25:54,019 --> 00:25:56,188
Here it comes.

470
00:26:06,632 --> 00:26:07,499
Huh?

471
00:26:12,438 --> 00:26:15,507
Sir! Sir!

472
00:26:15,574 --> 00:26:19,111
-Huh?
-Aren't you practicing yutnori?

473
00:26:19,178 --> 00:26:22,548
Practice? I don't need to.

474
00:26:23,315 --> 00:26:25,517
Why? Don't tell me you gave up already?

475
00:26:25,584 --> 00:26:28,253
I said I don't need to. Go on.

476
00:26:37,162 --> 00:26:39,498
Since teamwork is the whole point
of the township games,

477
00:26:39,565 --> 00:26:41,533
this 10-person 11-legged race

478
00:26:41,600 --> 00:26:43,535
-is worth the most points, right?
-Yes!

479
00:26:43,602 --> 00:26:44,670
Stay sharp, everyone.

480
00:26:44,736 --> 00:26:45,871
Just like we practiced.

481
00:26:45,938 --> 00:26:47,806
Ready, go!

482
00:26:47,873 --> 00:26:50,275
-One, two, one, two!
-Forward!

483
00:26:50,342 --> 00:26:52,177
One, two, one, two!

484
00:26:52,244 --> 00:26:53,779
-Hey, hey, hey, hey!
-One, two, one, two!

485
00:26:53,846 --> 00:26:55,547
What the heck is this?

486
00:26:59,184 --> 00:27:00,786
What happened?

487
00:27:03,522 --> 00:27:05,824
Can't you all even stay in step
with each other?

488
00:27:05,891 --> 00:27:08,093
You have the coordination
of grade-schoolers, seriously.

489
00:27:08,160 --> 00:27:11,930
What? Hey, you punk!
We're doing our best here!

490
00:27:11,997 --> 00:27:13,432
Is that any way to talk?

491
00:27:13,499 --> 00:27:15,634
You're bad at it, so I'm saying so.

492
00:27:15,701 --> 00:27:17,703
Even snot-nosed grade-schoolers
can do this.

493
00:27:17,769 --> 00:27:20,172
What? Hey, punk, have you lost your mind?

494
00:27:20,239 --> 00:27:21,507
Save it.

495
00:27:21,573 --> 00:27:23,475
I've been thinking about this,

496
00:27:23,542 --> 00:27:25,677
and no matter how much we practice,
this is hopeless.

497
00:27:25,744 --> 00:27:28,747
Just make up the numbers for us,

498
00:27:28,814 --> 00:27:31,016
and we'll win the whole thing for you.

499
00:27:31,083 --> 00:27:32,251
Make up the num…

500
00:27:32,317 --> 00:27:34,286
Listen to the nerve of this jerk!

501
00:27:34,353 --> 00:27:37,956
Fine, since we're like grade-schoolers,
we'll sit this out.

502
00:27:38,023 --> 00:27:40,893
Let's see how well you talented
young guys do on your own!

503
00:27:40,959 --> 00:27:42,294
I'm out! I quit!

504
00:27:42,361 --> 00:27:44,496
-Yun-hui, I'm out too.
-Where are you going?

505
00:27:44,563 --> 00:27:46,598
Kid, that's no way to talk to people.

506
00:27:46,665 --> 00:27:48,433
-Uncle, what's wrong with you?
-Let go, let go. Forget it.

507
00:27:48,500 --> 00:27:50,602
That young punk, seriously…

508
00:27:50,669 --> 00:27:53,071
You need to practice first!
Where are you going?

509
00:27:53,138 --> 00:27:54,039
Sang-deuk, hurry!

510
00:27:54,106 --> 00:27:55,674
Sang-deuk…

511
00:28:00,946 --> 00:28:02,915
Hey! What on earth are you doing?

512
00:28:02,981 --> 00:28:05,384
Forget it, just let them go.

513
00:28:05,450 --> 00:28:07,286
We're better off on our own.

514
00:28:07,352 --> 00:28:09,321
Better my foot! Look how many events

515
00:28:09,388 --> 00:28:11,056
there are. Will you guys do them all?

516
00:28:11,123 --> 00:28:13,392
There are event limits per person
and age limits too!

517
00:28:13,458 --> 00:28:18,263
Seriously, a local sports day
has all kinds of crappy rules.

518
00:28:18,864 --> 00:28:21,166
Hurry up and go apologize
to the elders right now!

519
00:28:21,233 --> 00:28:23,235
Forget it, I wasn't even wrong.

520
00:28:23,302 --> 00:28:25,871
Fine, do whatever you want!
Do as you please!

521
00:28:25,938 --> 00:28:29,708
Instead, your promise to go back
to Seoul if we don't win…

522
00:28:29,775 --> 00:28:31,410
Don't you forget it.

523
00:28:31,476 --> 00:28:32,978
That infuriating jerk, swear to God.

524
00:28:37,182 --> 00:28:38,817
Did she just eat me alive?

525
00:28:40,786 --> 00:28:42,321
Come on!

526
00:28:47,392 --> 00:28:49,328
This watermelon is so ripe.

527
00:28:51,063 --> 00:28:53,665
-Smells great.
-Min-ho, let's eat some watermelon.

528
00:28:58,103 --> 00:29:00,205
Where do you think you're reaching?

529
00:29:00,272 --> 00:29:02,975
I said room and board,
not snacks.

530
00:29:03,041 --> 00:29:05,944
Seriously, you fobbed us off
with ramen for lunch and dinner,

531
00:29:06,011 --> 00:29:07,312
and we can't get one slice?

532
00:29:07,379 --> 00:29:09,181
If you'd care to have this one slice,

533
00:29:09,248 --> 00:29:11,550
go apologize to the villagers
right now.

534
00:29:11,617 --> 00:29:13,485
You're being so petty, seriously.

535
00:29:13,552 --> 00:29:15,387
Blackmailing me with food, seriously.

536
00:29:15,454 --> 00:29:18,590
This is so petty and humiliating,
I'm taking a slice!

537
00:29:18,657 --> 00:29:20,292
Gosh, hey, hey, hey!

538
00:29:22,928 --> 00:29:24,663
What's this?

539
00:29:24,730 --> 00:29:25,831
Who are these people?

540
00:29:26,898 --> 00:29:29,334
He's a guy I know
who used to live here,

541
00:29:29,401 --> 00:29:30,802
and his friends, Hong-gu.

542
00:29:30,869 --> 00:29:34,773
Wait, the guys who killed Kkotdori?

543
00:29:37,442 --> 00:29:39,778
Their house burned down
completely to ashes,

544
00:29:39,845 --> 00:29:41,947
so they're staying with us for a bit.

545
00:29:42,014 --> 00:29:43,649
Are you crazy?

546
00:29:43,715 --> 00:29:46,118
After everything you went through
because of these guys,

547
00:29:46,184 --> 00:29:48,186
I'll never allow it!

548
00:29:48,253 --> 00:29:49,888
Get out right now.

549
00:29:49,955 --> 00:29:52,991
Who might this feisty little kid be?

550
00:29:54,426 --> 00:29:57,296
-He's my brother.
-Your brother?

551
00:29:57,362 --> 00:29:59,097
-Yes.
-You had a younger brother?

552
00:29:59,164 --> 00:30:00,565
Well, yes.

553
00:30:00,632 --> 00:30:03,335
That's none of your business.

554
00:30:04,036 --> 00:30:06,638
Get out right now, hurry.

555
00:30:06,705 --> 00:30:09,241
I've been letting this slide, and now

556
00:30:09,308 --> 00:30:12,077
some little punk is glaring straight

557
00:30:12,144 --> 00:30:15,614
into his elders' eyes?
Are you asking for it?

558
00:30:23,021 --> 00:30:24,856
Leave while I'm still asking nicely.

559
00:30:27,526 --> 00:30:29,828
-Gosh, Park Hong-gu, come here.
-Let go!

560
00:30:29,895 --> 00:30:32,497
-You're driving me crazy, come here.
-Let go of me!

561
00:30:32,564 --> 00:30:34,966
I'll explain everything,
so let's go inside. Come on.

562
00:30:35,033 --> 00:30:36,234
Let go, jeez!

563
00:30:39,805 --> 00:30:42,574
Must be his youth,
he sure has bold spirit.

564
00:30:42,641 --> 00:30:44,943
Speaking so formally to a high schooler…

565
00:30:49,348 --> 00:30:51,983
Did Yun-hui always have
such a young brother?

566
00:30:52,050 --> 00:30:55,587
Wait, didn't she call him
Park Hong-gu earlier?

567
00:30:55,654 --> 00:30:56,655
Isn't she a Kang?

568
00:30:56,722 --> 00:30:58,123
My older brother…

569
00:30:58,890 --> 00:31:01,393
I mean, Yun-hui's dad,

570
00:31:01,460 --> 00:31:04,062
moved down here and remarried
Hong-gu's mom.

571
00:31:06,164 --> 00:31:08,700
So they're not biological siblings?

572
00:31:09,935 --> 00:31:12,904
Where are her parents?
I don't think I've seen them.

573
00:31:13,872 --> 00:31:16,241
They passed away.

574
00:31:16,308 --> 00:31:18,377
At the exact same time in a car crash.

575
00:31:18,443 --> 00:31:20,112
What?

576
00:31:20,178 --> 00:31:21,680
How did that…

577
00:31:21,747 --> 00:31:25,517
They were driving to Seoul
to sell vegetables when a dump truck…

578
00:31:26,385 --> 00:31:29,755
So overnight, Yun-hui became
the head of the house.

579
00:31:29,821 --> 00:31:32,457
Taking care of Hong-gu and Min-ho,

580
00:31:32,524 --> 00:31:35,594
our Yun-hui went through so much.

581
00:31:36,561 --> 00:31:37,529
I see.

582
00:31:37,596 --> 00:31:40,031
Anyway, did sports day practice
go well today?

583
00:31:40,098 --> 00:31:41,900
It's a total bust, completely hopeless.

584
00:31:41,967 --> 00:31:43,902
Everyone has zero athleticism.

585
00:31:43,969 --> 00:31:46,938
What's the big deal about
a country sports day

586
00:31:47,005 --> 00:31:48,740
that everyone's risking their lives?

587
00:31:48,807 --> 00:31:51,877
Even Yun-hui, what's the big deal
about a mere Village Head title?

588
00:31:51,943 --> 00:31:55,514
To Yun-hui, it's not a mere
Village Head title.

589
00:31:56,281 --> 00:31:57,983
She lost her parents at a young age,

590
00:31:58,049 --> 00:32:00,952
and got pregnant without a husband,

591
00:32:01,019 --> 00:32:04,156
so imagine how much people
pointed fingers at her here.

592
00:32:04,222 --> 00:32:07,025
Then she finally earned
the villagers' respect,

593
00:32:07,092 --> 00:32:08,760
and they made her Village Head.

594
00:32:09,428 --> 00:32:12,130
She wouldn't want to step down
so easily like this.

595
00:32:12,197 --> 00:32:15,734
So please help our Yun-hui out.

596
00:32:15,801 --> 00:32:17,569
Please, I'm asking you.

597
00:32:27,145 --> 00:32:29,381
I thought she was just a crazy woman,

598
00:32:29,448 --> 00:32:31,550
but she's had a really stormy life.

599
00:32:34,319 --> 00:32:37,155
Right? It's on your mind too, Han-cheol?

600
00:32:38,290 --> 00:32:40,725
It's really weighing on my mind.

601
00:32:41,827 --> 00:32:43,462
Why on earth…

602
00:32:43,528 --> 00:32:46,665
did I have to poop right there
and then?

603
00:32:47,966 --> 00:32:50,268
-That's what bothered you?
-Anyway, what do we do?

604
00:32:50,769 --> 00:32:52,537
The villagers are all mad
because of you,

605
00:32:52,604 --> 00:32:54,272
so no one will show up
for practice.

606
00:32:54,339 --> 00:32:57,409
Whatever. I don't care if they come.

607
00:32:59,211 --> 00:33:01,880
Maybe it's from eating ramen all day,

608
00:33:01,947 --> 00:33:04,416
but there's a war in my stomach,
a total war.

609
00:33:04,483 --> 00:33:05,784
I'm hitting the restroom.

610
00:33:08,386 --> 00:33:09,421
Ugh, the smell.

611
00:33:10,589 --> 00:33:11,756
My legs hurt so bad.

612
00:33:11,823 --> 00:33:15,126
Get a bidet, at least.
A squat toilet? Seriously, a squat toilet?

613
00:33:23,301 --> 00:33:24,936
Hey, kid!

614
00:33:29,040 --> 00:33:30,642
Why are you up so late?

615
00:33:30,709 --> 00:33:33,812
I'm practicing for the talent show
at the sports day.

616
00:33:33,879 --> 00:33:35,947
They even do junk like that
at a sports day?

617
00:33:36,748 --> 00:33:39,351
It's a total hodgepodge, a real mess.

618
00:33:39,417 --> 00:33:42,954
I have to practice if I want
to win first place in the talent show!

619
00:33:43,021 --> 00:33:47,559
You said our village has to win
so my mom can stay the Village Head.

620
00:33:47,626 --> 00:33:49,160
What?

621
00:33:49,227 --> 00:33:50,829
So you're doing all this

622
00:33:50,896 --> 00:33:53,498
just so your mom can stay
the Village Head?

623
00:33:54,666 --> 00:33:56,301
What is a Village Head, anyway?

624
00:33:56,368 --> 00:33:59,104
The Prime Minister?
The UN Secretary-General?

625
00:33:59,170 --> 00:34:01,940
Why is everyone, from adults to kids,

626
00:34:02,007 --> 00:34:04,042
acting like being Village Head
is life or death?

627
00:34:04,109 --> 00:34:07,045
I told all my friends
my mom is the Village Head.

628
00:34:07,112 --> 00:34:09,514
I bragged about it so much.

629
00:34:09,581 --> 00:34:11,883
If she quits as Village Head,

630
00:34:12,384 --> 00:34:15,620
they'll tease me again like before.

631
00:34:15,687 --> 00:34:17,689
That my mom's unwed…

632
00:34:17,756 --> 00:34:20,792
and I'm a dummy who doesn't know his dad.

633
00:34:23,128 --> 00:34:26,765
What kind of awful people
say such nasty things?

634
00:34:26,831 --> 00:34:28,633
Did you just let that slide?

635
00:34:28,700 --> 00:34:31,836
You should've punched them
right in the gut, bam!

636
00:34:31,903 --> 00:34:36,508
Mister, don't you realize that violence
is never the answer?

637
00:34:38,310 --> 00:34:40,111
Please grow up.

638
00:34:44,583 --> 00:34:46,484
Are you telling me to grow up?

639
00:34:47,586 --> 00:34:49,521
Like mother, like son.

640
00:35:05,236 --> 00:35:06,304
Hey, kid.

641
00:35:06,371 --> 00:35:08,640
Think you'll win first place
like that?

642
00:35:08,707 --> 00:35:12,344
You really think pure innocence
still works on an audience?

643
00:35:12,410 --> 00:35:16,014
These days, just being cute and young…

644
00:35:16,081 --> 00:35:19,050
Nobody hands out first place
out of charity in this world.

645
00:35:19,117 --> 00:35:20,952
Then what should I do?

646
00:35:21,019 --> 00:35:23,488
Shock! Provocation! Sensation!

647
00:35:23,555 --> 00:35:26,124
You need a shocking performance.

648
00:35:26,191 --> 00:35:27,325
What's that?

649
00:35:33,331 --> 00:35:36,835
Miss, try some of this corn.

650
00:35:39,404 --> 00:35:40,939
Is she asleep?

651
00:35:41,006 --> 00:35:43,775
Oh dear, she must be tired
from painting all day.

652
00:36:18,410 --> 00:36:19,411
Not here either.

653
00:36:19,477 --> 00:36:21,746
Is it really buried here or not?

654
00:36:24,949 --> 00:36:26,584
Wait…

655
00:36:28,186 --> 00:36:32,724
Was that jerk even telling the truth?

656
00:36:37,062 --> 00:36:41,332
You need to know how pure
and devoted my love is.

657
00:36:41,833 --> 00:36:46,371
Listen, I'm skipping the country soon.

658
00:36:46,438 --> 00:36:50,575
I'll take care of you for life.

659
00:36:50,642 --> 00:36:54,212
Sure, sure, just drink up, honey.

660
00:36:54,279 --> 00:36:56,047
Truth is…

661
00:36:56,114 --> 00:37:00,385
I'm an aide to a pretty famous
assemblyman.

662
00:37:01,853 --> 00:37:02,721
Really?

663
00:37:02,787 --> 00:37:04,889
You know what a slush fund is, right?

664
00:37:04,956 --> 00:37:08,326
I manage that jerk's slush fund.

665
00:37:08,393 --> 00:37:12,597
And I took part of that slush fund…

666
00:37:12,664 --> 00:37:15,467
and stashed it away.

667
00:37:15,533 --> 00:37:17,502
Really? How much?

668
00:37:18,737 --> 00:37:23,208
Five billion won, all in cold, hard cash.

669
00:37:23,975 --> 00:37:27,912
Five billion? Where did you hide
five billion in cash?

670
00:37:33,051 --> 00:37:36,654
I can't tell you that. No way, no how.

671
00:37:36,721 --> 00:37:39,624
True, stuff like that is a secret.

672
00:37:40,191 --> 00:37:43,228
I also have a huge pile of gold bars…

673
00:37:43,294 --> 00:37:45,764
stashed at my place, this big.

674
00:37:45,830 --> 00:37:47,632
I'm serious, you little brat.

675
00:37:47,699 --> 00:37:51,669
Think I'm chugging this pricey booze
just to joke around?

676
00:37:53,071 --> 00:37:54,139
Fine.

677
00:37:54,205 --> 00:37:57,709
It's in Soul-myeon, Hadurok…

678
00:38:01,946 --> 00:38:04,816
Hadurok-ri.

679
00:38:05,583 --> 00:38:07,719
I buried it in a little field there.

680
00:38:08,286 --> 00:38:09,988
SUBWAY ENTRANCE

681
00:38:10,655 --> 00:38:12,657
Five billion in cash, my foot.

682
00:38:12,724 --> 00:38:15,293
Like I haven't seen a dozen creeps
just like him.

683
00:38:16,261 --> 00:38:18,496
How long do I have to live like this?

684
00:38:19,464 --> 00:38:22,500
Wait, my new product proposal!

685
00:38:23,034 --> 00:38:24,969
Jeez, I left it behind again.

686
00:38:25,937 --> 00:38:27,806
This is so annoying.

687
00:38:36,014 --> 00:38:37,682
Hey, who are you guys?

688
00:38:37,749 --> 00:38:39,717
-Who are you?
-Shut up and get in.

689
00:38:39,784 --> 00:38:41,486
Hey, help me!

690
00:38:41,553 --> 00:38:43,288
Hey, call the police!

691
00:38:43,354 --> 00:38:44,989
Police!

692
00:38:45,857 --> 00:38:47,292
Talk and you'll live.

693
00:38:47,358 --> 00:38:49,594
So just tell us now.
Where's the money?

694
00:38:49,661 --> 00:38:51,896
I don't know what you mean…

695
00:38:51,963 --> 00:38:53,731
We know you stole it, you bastard.

696
00:38:53,798 --> 00:38:55,466
Spill it if you want to live.

697
00:38:55,533 --> 00:38:59,070
I told you, I don't know anything!

698
00:38:59,137 --> 00:39:00,805
-You don't know?
-I don't!

699
00:39:05,043 --> 00:39:06,945
Why make this hard on yourself?

700
00:39:07,011 --> 00:39:09,147
Talk. Where's the money?

701
00:39:09,214 --> 00:39:13,017
Okay, okay. Well, the thing is,
it's…

702
00:39:13,084 --> 00:39:15,486
O… over there!

703
00:39:15,553 --> 00:39:16,921
Is that bastard nuts?

704
00:39:27,699 --> 00:39:29,868
Hey, mister! Mister!

705
00:39:29,934 --> 00:39:31,903
Why did you jump out like that?

706
00:39:31,970 --> 00:39:32,904
Open your eyes!

707
00:39:32,971 --> 00:39:34,405
C… call someone!

708
00:39:34,472 --> 00:39:36,374
-Call 119, hurry!
-This is nuts.

709
00:39:36,441 --> 00:39:38,176
Call the police, hurry!

710
00:39:39,477 --> 00:39:41,546
There's been an accident here!

711
00:39:42,280 --> 00:39:44,749
-We're… we're at…
-What do I do?

712
00:39:44,816 --> 00:39:46,885
What on earth just happened?

713
00:39:48,186 --> 00:39:51,155
Then what he said earlier was all true…

714
00:39:52,357 --> 00:39:54,792
Five billion won in cash?

715
00:39:56,661 --> 00:39:58,897
Where did he say it was?

716
00:40:00,265 --> 00:40:02,500
Ha… Ha…

717
00:40:03,501 --> 00:40:04,969
Ha…

718
00:40:05,036 --> 00:40:08,339
HARD ROCK CAFE

719
00:40:08,406 --> 00:40:10,909
HARD ROCK CAFE

720
00:40:12,243 --> 00:40:13,444
That's it!

721
00:40:13,511 --> 00:40:15,513
Hadurok-ri!

722
00:40:23,488 --> 00:40:25,356
No, it's definitely here somewhere.

723
00:40:25,957 --> 00:40:28,126
Whatever, just dig! Keep digging!

724
00:40:49,113 --> 00:40:54,185
Though we have lived

725
00:40:55,853 --> 00:40:59,524
Apart like this

726
00:41:02,393 --> 00:41:07,298
Have you forgotten me

727
00:41:08,533 --> 00:41:13,404
And my burning eyes?

728
00:41:15,540 --> 00:41:18,109
Have you forgotten

729
00:41:18,176 --> 00:41:21,479
My name from back then

730
00:41:22,380 --> 00:41:27,051
And our beautiful memories?

731
00:41:37,261 --> 00:41:38,596
What are you up to?

732
00:41:39,564 --> 00:41:42,633
He just fell asleep.
Shh, keep it down.

733
00:41:46,170 --> 00:41:49,974
How do you know that song?
It's pretty old.

734
00:41:50,975 --> 00:41:53,811
It was my dad's favorite song.

735
00:41:53,878 --> 00:41:57,815
I heard it so much growing up
that I came to love it too.

736
00:41:58,583 --> 00:42:02,320
Funny enough, Min-ho sleeps so well
whenever he hears it too.

737
00:42:03,254 --> 00:42:05,523
Guess it really runs in the family.

738
00:42:07,959 --> 00:42:09,460
Why aren't you asleep?

739
00:42:10,528 --> 00:42:12,330
I can't sleep well. Insomnia.

740
00:42:12,397 --> 00:42:16,334
Insomnia? Gosh, what a spoiled problem.

741
00:42:17,335 --> 00:42:19,670
Do a little more farm work out here.

742
00:42:19,737 --> 00:42:23,007
You'll fall sound asleep
the second your head hits the floor.

743
00:42:25,043 --> 00:42:28,012
Then put me to sleep too
until that happens.

744
00:42:29,180 --> 00:42:30,281
What are you doing?

745
00:42:30,348 --> 00:42:31,716
Move! Get off!

746
00:42:31,783 --> 00:42:35,286
You look normal,
but you're a total nutcase.

747
00:42:35,853 --> 00:42:37,555
I get that a lot.

748
00:42:37,622 --> 00:42:39,457
Come on, sing me a lullaby.

749
00:42:40,124 --> 00:42:41,826
You crazy jerk.

750
00:42:41,893 --> 00:42:43,961
Do I look like I have
nothing better to do?

751
00:42:44,028 --> 00:42:45,329
Move!

752
00:42:46,397 --> 00:42:47,265
You'll be sorry…

753
00:42:47,331 --> 00:42:48,633
What'll I regret?

754
00:42:48,699 --> 00:42:50,334
What? What'll you do?

755
00:42:52,136 --> 00:42:54,472
His name's Min-ho, right?

756
00:42:54,539 --> 00:42:55,973
If he wakes, it's chaos. No.

757
00:42:56,040 --> 00:42:58,709
Then hurry and sing to me,
or else I really will…

758
00:42:58,776 --> 00:43:02,313
Have you forgotten me

759
00:43:03,915 --> 00:43:08,386
Those burning eyes

760
00:43:10,721 --> 00:43:13,691
Have you forgotten

761
00:43:13,758 --> 00:43:16,461
My name from back then

762
00:43:17,361 --> 00:43:22,033
And those beautiful memories?

763
00:43:25,002 --> 00:43:30,441
Though we were in love

764
00:43:31,742 --> 00:43:36,380
We couldn't even meet

765
00:43:39,684 --> 00:43:44,322
Parted from each other

766
00:43:46,491 --> 00:43:50,461
We've lived on like this

767
00:43:54,332 --> 00:43:58,269
EXCELLENT SOULS

768
00:44:00,872 --> 00:44:04,475
Man, shoveling all day made
every bone in my body ache.

769
00:44:04,542 --> 00:44:05,710
Me too, me too.

770
00:44:09,514 --> 00:44:11,215
What's he doing?

771
00:44:17,388 --> 00:44:21,526
Gosh, the local mosquitoes
had another feast on you.

772
